  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["U2 (display, ER-OLED0.96-1W / SSD1306, on display.kicad_sch)"],
      "pins": ["U2.10 (BS0)", "U2.11 (BS1)", "U2.12 (BS2)"],
      "nets": ["BS0", "BS1", "BS2", "VCC", "GND"],
      "observed": "On display.kicad_sch the SSD1306 interface-select pins are strapped to the wrong rails: BS0 (pin 10) is wired to the VCC rail, BS1 (pin 11) is wired to the GND symbol, and BS2 (pin 12) is wired to the VCC rail, i.e. BS[2:0] = 1,0,1.",
      "expected": "The specification states the display is configured for I2C by hard-wiring BS0 (pin 10) -> GND, BS1 (pin 11) -> VCC, BS2 (pin 12) -> GND (BS[2:0]=0,1,0), and the MCU drives it over a 2-wire bus (PB13=DISP_SCL on D0, PB14=DISP_SDA on D1/D2). The strap pins must be tied to the opposite rails.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "BS0 (pin 10) -> GND; BS1 (pin 11) -> VCC; BS2 (pin 12) -> GND ... That BS2,BS1,BS0 = 0,1,0 strapping ... is the SSD1306's documented I2C-mode pin configuration"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "display.kicad_sch (page 5): BS0 pin 10 wire joins the VCC rail at top-right; BS1 pin 11 wire joins the GND symbol; BS2 pin 12 wire joins the VCC rail"}
      ],
      "impact": "The OLED driver is left in a non-I2C (SPI/parallel) interface mode, so the MCU's two-wire signals on D0/D1/D2 are not interpreted as SCL/SDA and the display will not communicate or show information.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The one behaviour-changing deviation I can read off the drawing is the SSD1306 interface-select strapping on display.kicad_sch: BS0/BS1/BS2 are tied to VCC/GND/VCC instead of the GND/VCC/GND (0,1,0) I2C strap the spec requires, which would put the OLED in the wrong bus mode. Other apparent differences from the spec (U3<->U4, A1<->A2, R/C renumbering) are just reference-designator renumbering in this build and do not alter electrical behaviour, so they are not reported."
}

